<para id="X39400000ID00QC" category="C" type-id="304N1" name-id="161XC-00" from="200612">
<dtccode>B2281</dtccode>
<dtcname>P Signal Malfunction</dtcname>
<subpara id="X39400000ID00QC_10" type-id="31" category="03" proc-id="RM0550J___00004A200000">
<name>Circuit Description</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<list1 type="nonmark">
<item>
<ptxt>This DTC is output when there is a mismatch between the signal on the direct line in the circuit between the instrument panel J/B assembly (main body ECU) and the shift lock control unit (shift lock ECU), and the signal on the multiplex communication line (CAN) between the instrument panel J/B assembly (main body ECU) and the engine control computer (engine ECU).</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
<atten3>
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>When using the TaSCAN with the IG OFF, repeatedly turn any door courtesy light switch ON and OFF (at intervals of 1.5 seconds or less) until communication between the TaSCAN and the vehicle starts.</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>The Smart Entry &amp; Start System (start system) has functions that use multiplex communication. First, follow "How to Proceed with Troubleshooting" and confirm that there is no malfunction in the communication system before proceeding with troubleshooting.</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</atten3>
<atten4>
<ptxt>When the instrument panel J/B assembly (main body ECU) is replaced with a new ECU and the battery negative terminal is connected, it enters the IG ON state. Also, when the battery is removed and reinstalled, the power source returns to the state it was in when the battery was removed.</ptxt>
</atten4>
